//api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T17:12:06Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T17:12:06Z","body":"[This static int](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2d113cc224cb9be07866d003819fcef2226a52ea/editor/editor_node.cpp#L5351) is used to track the number of steps in the current task. It has the comment \"All tasks run sequentially, so we can just keep a single counter\", but this isn't actually true. \n\n`editor_file_system.cpp:reimport_files` sets up [an initial reimport job here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2d113cc224cb9be07866d003819fcef2226a52ea/editor/file_system/editor_file_system.cpp#L3187) with the correct number of steps, but it ends up getting clobbered by [this signal emission](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2d113cc224cb9be07866d003819fcef2226a52ea/editor/file_system/editor_file_system.cpp#L3248) because [this code](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2d113cc224cb9be07866d003819fcef2226a52ea/editor/editor_node.cpp#L6576) ends up running as one of the connected functions.\n\nI'm not sure what a good fix is here, so I'll leave it for another contributor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3128202061/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3163963878","html_ur